# Edge case [D10, M]: node ids that look like checker prefixes or share prefixes (node, cap, zone_x, a, a1, a_1) and a group group_a. Checker nodeKey strips node-/cap- prefixes so aliasing is possible; a checker-id-collision false result would show here.
dir DOWN
group group_a "Group A" :blue {
  a[A]
  a1[A1]
}
node[Node]
cap[Cap]
zone_x[Zone X]
a_1[A underscore 1]
node -> cap : one
cap -> zone_x : two
zone_x -> a : three
a -> a1 : four
a1 -> a_1 : five
a_1 -> node : six
node -> a1 : seven
